<title>USA: U.S. meat output 0.9 pct above a week ago - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. meat output 0.9 pct above a week ago - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Red meat production for week ending Saturday, April 12, rose 0.9 at 793.6 million lbs.-USDA</p>
<p>WEEK ENDING/1  BEEF   CALF/VEAL   PORK/2 LAMB/MUTTON TOTALS/3</p>
<p>12-Apr-97	459.3     6.5	 323.2     4.6	793.6</p>
<p>05-Apr-97	452.3     6.5	 323.0     4.8	786.6</p>
<p>Change:	    1.6%    0.0%	  0.1%   -4.2%	0.9%</p>
<p>13-Apr-96	467.7     6.2	 330.6     5.6	810.1</p>
<p>Change:	   -1.8%    4.8%	 -2.2%  -17.9%	-2.0%</p>
<p>1997 YTD:     6816.0    94.6	4721.8    73.7    11706.1</p>
<p>1996 YTD:     7102.8   100.4	4975.3    84.3    12262.8</p>
<p>Change:	   -4.0%   -5.8%	 -5.1%  -12.6%	-4.5%</p>
<p>LIVESTOCK SLAUGHTER (HEAD)</p>
<p>WEEK ENDING   CATTLE    CALVES/VEALERS    HOGS     SHEEP/LAMBS</p>
